{"kind":"request","text":"claude: give gs the query capabilities that the AGENTS.md runbook currently reaches for jq to get. Hugh's framing on 2026-08-21: anything we filter with jq should be considered for a feature capability in the gs query instead. This is the companion to a4766266, the AGENTS.md cut, and the two are deliberately independent — neither gates the other, and the doc cut is not waiting on this.\n\nTHE ASYMMETRY, WHICH IS THE REAL DEFECT. gs status takes exactly three flags: --json, --all, --server. It has no selectors at all. So every question anyone asks of the log gets answered by dumping the whole projection and filtering it by hand. Meanwhile a real query layer already exists one level up: statusview.WorkQuery carries actor, lanes, statuses, a three-way stale filter, limit and cursor, and BuildWorkPage and BuildItemInspection implement it at internal/statusview/query.go:243 and :433. Both are reachable from the MCP adapter at cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:773 and :806 and from the resident at internal/service/server.go:270 and :300 — and from nowhere in cmd/gs. The CLI is the only consumer forced to hand-roll, and that is why the jq exists.\n\nSo most of this is reach, not invention. Condition 2 is the load-bearing one: expose the existing query through gs by calling the same builders. A second implementation of the same selectors would be exactly the duplication the round-two simplification survey is currently cataloguing, and I would rather not commission a new instance of it in the same week.\n\nWHAT THE FIVE JQ PROGRAMS ACTUALLY ASK FOR, so the surface is driven by real questions rather than guesses. AGENTS.md lines 166 and 288 select artifacts whose path is an exact string and which are not retired, the second to generate supersede acts for gs batch. Line 183 counts review requests that no effective verdict has settled, and separately asks which approved, ratified, non-world-stale heads are still not ancestors of main. Lines 318 and 351 walk provenance transitively — one to prove no live artifact still reaches an artifact at `.`, the other to measure how far a staleness wave reaches. Reduced to capabilities: artifacts selectable by path and state; provenance followed to closure rather than one hop; and an ancestry question gs is already equipped to answer, since validateMerge does exactly that check internally today.\n\ngs provenance already exists and takes one event, rendering a single hop. Extending it to a transitive walk is the smaller half of this; do not write a new closure algorithm beside it.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT ASKING FOR. Do not build a general query language. The test is that the runbook's five programs can be expressed as commands, plus the work-queue questions the MCP already answers. If a selector is not needed by one of those, leave it out — an unused flag is the same fluff in a different file. Condition 5 exists because a query surface that dumps everything when a selector matches everything has just moved the problem.\n\nSEQUENCING. Independent of a4766266. When this lands, the notes/ runbook file is the one place that needs rewriting to cite commands instead of jq, and that rewrite is a separate, small child — do not bundle it here.","body":{"conditions":"1. gs can answer, without jq, the questions the AGENTS.md runbook currently answers with jq: select artifacts by exact path and by live/retired/succeeded state; follow artifact provenance transitively rather than one hop; and report which approved heads are not ancestors of a named branch. 2. The existing statusview.WorkQuery selectors already reachable from MCP and the resident HTTP surface - actor, lanes, statuses, the three-way stale filter, limit and cursor - become reachable from the gs CLI too, through one shared code path rather than a second implementation. Reuse BuildWorkPage/BuildItemInspection; do not fork the query logic. 3. Output is machine-readable under --json and human-readable by default, and the JSON shape matches what the MCP work and inspect tools already return, so a caller learns one shape. 4. Nothing about the resident, MCP or HTTP surfaces changes behaviour; this is CLI reach, not a new query semantics. 5. Adversarial coverage for selector inputs: unknown path, unknown event, empty result, and a selector that matches everything, each producing a bounded honest answer rather than an error or an unbounded dump. 6. docs/reference/gs/status.md and any new page state the selectors, and docs/reference/architecture.md is updated in the same head if a layer contract moves. 7. make vet, make test, make race, make build, make docs, gofmt and diff-check pass at the exact head; artifacts at every maintained path the head changes; independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review before merge.","priority":"P2","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d","verified_at":"main e9288b18 on 2026-08-21"}}